# Everything under data/ is produced by running the pipeline, and most of it is not small. Most of that state no
# longer lives here at all: each match's analysis - segments, reports, replays, events, scans, caches - is saved
# beside the footage in an `analysis/` folder, so clearing, copying or moving the match takes its state along.
# What can still sit here:
#
#   games/      legacy manifests of combined multi-clip games; newer ones live with the analysis beside the clips
#   rosters/    team rosters: shirt number -> player name, typed once per team and reused across matches
#   videos/     local input footage (see the .gitignore in there)
#   models/     downloaded detector weights and saved calibrations (see the .gitignore in there)
#
# All of it can be rebuilt from the source video, so none of it is committed. Small hand-written inputs that live
# here - a saved calibration, a set of landmark annotations - are ignored too; force-add one if it is worth
# keeping, for example:
#
#   git add -f data/models/calibration_half_a.json
*
!.gitignore
